# R2 Data Lake & CDN Architecture

## Overview

Heavy analytics are offloaded from PostgreSQL to Apache Iceberg tables stored in Cloudflare R2, queried via R2 SQL. Static assets (avatars, PDFs, videos) are served through a CDN Worker on `cdn.sovereignsanctuary.net` with Smart Tiered Cache for near-zero repeated-read costs.

## Architecture

```
PostgreSQL (transactional OLTP)
  ↓ CDC Agent (60s poll)
Cloudflare Pipelines (HTTP ingest)
  ↓ sink (Parquet files)
R2 bucket: nate-analytics (Iceberg tables via Data Catalog)
  ↓
R2 SQL (distributed analytics queries)
  ↓
/api/analytics/* REST endpoints (admin dashboard)
```

```
R2 bucket: nate-vault (static assets)
  ↓
cdn.sovereignsanctuary.net Worker (nate-r2-cdn)
  ↓ Cache-Control: s-maxage=2592000
Cloudflare Smart Tiered Cache (upper-tier DC near R2)
  ↓
Cloudflare Edge (200+ DCs worldwide)
  ↓ cache HIT (99%+ after warmup)
Client browser
```

## 5 R2 Buckets

| Bucket | Purpose | CDN | Data Catalog |
|---|---|---|---|
| `nate-vault` | Avatars, PDFs, videos, exports, coach files | `cdn.sovereignsanctuary.net/vault/*` | Yes |
| `nate-analytics` | Iceberg tables (CDC from PostgreSQL) | `cdn.sovereignsanctuary.net/lake/*` | Yes |
| `nate-cold-archive` | Cold memory tier | No | No |
| `nate-heritage-vault` | Transgenerational legacy storage | No | No |
| `nate-warm-memory` | Warm memory tier | No | No |

## CDC Agent (`iceberg_cdc_agent.py`)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Cycle | 60 seconds |
| Tables | 10 (conversation_history, skyeye_activity, token_transactions, nevedal_metrics, wisdom_extractions, me2me_imprint_entries, skyeye_post_analytics, skyeye_notifications, coaching_sessions, skyeye_sessions) |
| Watermark table | `iceberg_cdc_watermarks` |
| Batch size | 500 rows per table per cycle |
| Encrypted content | Redacted (empty string) in CDC events |

The agent polls each table for rows newer than its watermark timestamp, pushes them as JSON events to Cloudflare Pipeline HTTP endpoints, and advances the watermark on success.

## R2 Analytics Service (`r2_analytics_service.py`)

Executes SQL queries against R2 Iceberg tables via the R2 SQL API. Falls back to PostgreSQL if R2 SQL is unavailable.

Pre-built queries:
- `conversation_volume(days)` — daily chat volume + word counts
- `token_usage_trends(days)` — daily token usage by source
- `coherence_trends(days)` — daily Nevedal metric averages + CEE windows
- `wisdom_insights(days)` — insight types + approval rates
- `social_engagement_trends(days)` — platform engagement metrics
- `coaching_session_stats(days)` — session status + revenue
- `cross_table_user_engagement(user_id)` — multi-table user profile

