## R2 CDN Worker (`cloudflare/workers/r2-cdn/`)

| Route | Bucket | Cache Profile |
|---|---|---|
| `/vault/*` | nate-vault | 30d edge / 7d browser (static), 1h/10m (exports) |
| `/lake/*` | nate-analytics | 24h edge / 1h browser (Parquet immutable) |
| `/health` | — | Health check |

## Smart Tiered Cache

Enabled at the zone level (sovereignsanctuary.net). Automatically picks the optimal upper-tier DC nearest to R2 data location (ENAM). Reduces origin pulls to R2 even for cache misses at the edge — the upper-tier DC absorbs them.

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` | Used by CDC agent for Pipeline HTTP endpoint |
| `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` | Auth for Pipelines + R2 SQL |
| `R2_CDN_BASE_URL` | `https://cdn.sovereignsanctuary.net` |
| `R2_ANALYTICS_WAREHOUSE` | R2 SQL warehouse ID |

## Rules

1. **Never query analytics tables directly from PostgreSQL in request handlers** — use the R2 analytics service which routes to R2 SQL.
2. **CDC agent handles encrypted content** — `conversation_history` rows with `content_encrypted = true` have `user_text` and `ai_text` redacted to empty strings in CDC events. The encrypted columns are never sent to R2.
3. **Iceberg tables are append-only** — the CDC agent only pushes INSERTs. Updates and deletes are not captured (PostgreSQL remains authoritative for live data).
4. **CDN URLs use `/vault/` prefix** — `get_cdn_url("avatars/foo.png")` returns `https://cdn.sovereignsanctuary.net/vault/avatars/foo.png`.
5. **The CDC agent gracefully degrades** — if `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` or `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` are not set, it logs a message and does not start.
6. **Backfill is idempotent** — resetting watermarks and re-pushing rows is safe because Pipeline sinks use append semantics.
7. **R2 SQL queries use the `sanctuary` namespace** — all tables are under `sanctuary.*` (e.g., `sanctuary.conversation_history`).
